Bug #4
Zip codes are not unique: Duplicates of already used zip codes are added to the available codes

Precondition: as a verified user

Steps to Reproduce:
    1. Send GET request to get the codes http://localhost:49000/zip-codes
    2. Verify "23456" is in the response
    3. Add a new user with the code: send POST request to http://localhost:49000/users, where body: {"age": 255, "name": "Tester22","sex": "MALE","zipCode":"23456"}
    4. Get a user to verify the code is added, GET request to http://localhost:49000/users
    5. Verify "23456" is in the response
    6. Try to add the same zip code: "23456", send POST request to http://localhost:49000/zip-codes/expand, body: ["23456"]
    7. Verify the response
Actual result: "23456" is in the response, so duplicate in use can be added to available zip codes
Expected result: When zip code is in use, it should not be possible to add the same code to available ones

